  <main>
    <section class="card span12">
      <p class="proof-note"><b>Testing, not proof.</b> This page logs every solar wind speed spike and every U.S. volcano alert-level change,
        using a rule fixed before looking at the results. A match only means the two happened within <span id="win">48</span> hours of each other.
        Spikes and alert changes are both common, so some matches happen by pure chance. The tally below shows how many matches chance alone
        would give. Only a long record that beats chance by a wide margin would be worth a closer look, and even then it would not show cause.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="card span8">
      <h2>Timeline</h2>
      <div class="chart-box"><canvas id="chart"></canvas></div>
      <p class="note">Line: hourly median solar wind speed (km/s). Gold diamonds: spike starts. Triangles: volcano alert changes, colored by the new aviation color code (pointing up = raised, down = lowered). Times are Eastern (24-hour).</p>
    </section>

    <section class="card span4">
      <h2>Running tally</h2>
      <div class="stats" id="tally"></div>
      <p class="note" id="tally-note"></p>
      <h2 style="margin-top:16px">Elevated now (USGS)</h2>
      <div id="elevated" class="note">Loading…</div>
    </section>

    <section class="card span12">
      <h2>Volcano alert changes</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table id="changes"><thead><tr><th>When (ET)</th><th>Volcano</th><th>Observatory</th><th>Change</th><th>Nearest spike</th><th>Match (±<span class="winh">48</span> h)</th><th>Notice</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    </section>

    <section class="card span12">
      <h2>Solar wind spikes</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table id="spikes"><thead><tr><th>Start (ET)</th><th>Baseline</th><th>Speed</th><th>Rise</th><th>24 h peak</th><th>Rule</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    </section>

    <section class="card span12" id="method">
      <h2>Method</h2>
      <p class="note">Spike rule, match window and chance calculation are fixed in advance. <a href="methods.html">See full method →</a></p>
